==Trivia==
* When defeated, the Maids in the 5-Maid Knockout Exact-Turn Attack Challenge all say the same—"You're so strong!"—adding only an additional exclamation mark for each maid defeated.
** One of those Maids is Elena (Japanese: ヘレン ''Helen''), who reappears in [[Kalos hotels]] in {{g|X and Y}}, offering to [[In-game trade#Pokémon X and Y|trade]] the player an {{p|Eevee}} for any Pokémon. The names are the same in Japanese, English, and Korean, but different in French, German, Italian, and Spanish.
* When a Maid is battled at the {{gdis|Battle Frontier|IV}}, she will be shown as a {{tc|Waitress}} in {{2v2|Diamond|Pearl}}, as the Maid class did not exist in those versions.
* Maids appeared in the [[Battle Pike]] in Pokémon Emerald, although they cannot be battled.
* In the [[Battle Chateau]], Maid Julia is shown to be a robot, making her the first robotic Trainer in the [[core series]] games.

